 "_doc": "Every ffmpeg/ffprobe option, filter (with the filter options used), encoder and format the shipped code passes, with the release each first shipped in (`min`, read from the ffmpeg source tags 4.4 to 9.0; \"4.4\" = already in 4.4, the oldest checked). workflows/test_ffmpeg_vocab.py holds it to the code both ways and checks every entry against the ffmpeg on PATH: missing or deprecated fails. `floor` is the highest min outside the `fallback` entries (each is used only where its probe finds it): the oldest ffmpeg the shipped code runs on. `os` entries are checked on that OS only; `fallback` names the one file that may use an option, and only on an ffmpeg without its replacement (`when_missing`) or where that file's probe picks it (`picked_by`, a function in workflows/ffmpeg_compat.py). `lean_build_gaps` are filters Homebrew's lean ffmpeg lacks (ffmpeg-full has them), listed so the scrape still sees one if code starts using it.",
